This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
freenode.net.  Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.

[1]: putting on a ring of levitation while standing on a sink should
not let you levitate in the first place, thus doing no damage.
--dtriscuit

[2]: Make people in pits near-immune to projectiles (~80% chance to
miss), so that rangers and wizards can dig down to form bunkers. Hell
yeah, son. --Azeral

[3]: cursed+confused ?oLight makes the whole current level dark
--Xarann

[4]: The color for the floating eyes needs to be lighter --Gaulgath

[5]: rubbing a stone against a /oPoly should polymorph the stone
--Botje

[6]: Lizard scale mail - Lizards have a 25% chance of dropping scales
when killed. Lizard scales are stackable and wearable; if you are
wearing 5 or more, it may be enchanted up to mail status. Lizard scale
mail has the same protection as an orcish chain mail, and provides
stoning resistance. --TheShrewdDude_

[7]: Even before the top of Rodney's tower, there ought to be another
fake tower without a moat. This tower has a non-secret door, as well as
a vampire lord and hell hound inside. Between them sits Fake Rodney: a
doppelganger wearing an amulet of unchanging. --TheShrewdDude

[8]: Helmet description: opera mask.  Wear with a cloak of description
"opera cloak" for a bonus or penalty (and YAFMs when hallucinating).
--Grunt

[9]: Having many uranium wands in your inventory abuses your
constitution. Having a lot of them kills you. "Your uranium wands get
hot.". "Joe, killed by elementary nuclear physics". --Avian

[10]: But if you happen to be wearing an "oLS, it's a crude but
effective form of crowd control. --cjeris

[11]: if female, t-shirts should give a boost to charisma when recently
gotten wet (pool of water, rust trap, etc) --Smeghead_

[12]: Zombies should be greedy for mummy wrappings. If there is one
nearby, it should try to wear it and turn into the appropriate type of
mummy. Mummies should have greater bonuses over zombies for this
reason. --TheShrewdDude

[13]: squeaky doors that act like squeaky board traps when you open
them --iank

[14]: The 'G' command should follow paths in the gehennom mazes along
their twists and turns until you encounter an actual fork, monster or
object. --Smello

[15]: pushing boulders into water with 'submerged' (hidden, unknown,
whatever) water creatures should hurt/kill them. --iank

[16]: Tins can contain spam. maybe YAFM when hallu? --Botje

[17]: Form of item erosion: denting.  "You see here a thoroughly dented
pot." --Grunt

[18]: Amulet of the prism. Grants reflection with the special trait
that you get one reflection for each distinct source of reflection you
have. --cjeris

[19]: A Unicode version. A-Za-z just isn't enough. --nornagon

